silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_02_free_category_monad_sections_04_mittens_in_the_monad_concrete_anchors a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "MittensColimitInMonadAlgebraConcreteAnchorsExample" .
silm:instances_papers_10_graph_knowledge_graph_category_chapters_02_free_category_monad_sections_04_mittens_in_the_monad_concrete_anchors silm:hasExample "In 'MittensColimitInMonadAlgebraConcreteAnchors', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, The shape of the Mittens cocone. Objects: type, evidence, taxonomy, quality, measurement, microchip, process. Arrows include any compatibility-condition arrows between legs (e.g., the taxonomy leg and the type leg both target into D_Mittens but at distinct source vertices). ; also, j=type yields DomesticCat with arrow rdf:type; j=evidence yields VetRecord77 with arrow is_about; j=taxonomy yields the row Felis catus / TSN 183798 with the taxonomy source arrow; j=quality yields BodyMassQuality77 with arrow bearer_of; j=microchip yields MicrochipIdentifier9 with arrow has_microchip. ; also, lambda_type : DomesticCat -> Mittens is the rdf:type arrow read backwards (Mittens is_a DomesticCat). lambda_evidence : VetRecord77 -> Mittens is the is_about arrow. Each lambda_j is an equivalence class of paths in C_G (after equiv_E quotient). ." .
